=== width 80
[bold,italic,double-underline]frobnicate[]

A small command line tool that [bold]frobnicates[] files, [italic]quickly[] and with [yellow]zero[]
configuration. See [underline]https://example.com/frobnicate[] for the full manual, or ask in
the chat.

[bold,underline]Installation[]

Install from source with a recent Rust toolchain:

  cargo install frobnicate
  frobnicate[cyan] --version[]

Prebuilt binaries are available for these platforms:

• Linux, x86_64 and aarch64
• macOS, Apple silicon and Intel
• Windows, x86_64 only
  • requires the Visual C++ runtime
  • no ARM build yet

[bold,underline]Usage[]

  [yellow]frobnicate [OPTIONS] <FILE>...[]

┌─────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────┐
│ [bold]  Option   [] │ [bold]               Meaning                [] │ [bold]Default[] │
├─────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────┤
│ [yellow]-q[], [yellow]--quiet[] │ Print nothing except errors            │   off   │
├─────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────┤
│ [yellow]-j[], [yellow]--jobs[]  │ Number of parallel jobs                │    [yellow]4[]    │
├─────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────┤
│ [yellow]--dry-run[]   │ Show what would change, change nothing │   off   │
└─────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────┘

[bold]Exit codes[]

1. [yellow]0[] when every file was processed.
2. [yellow]1[] when at least one file failed.
3. [yellow]2[] for invalid arguments.

[cyan]│ [][bold]Note[] Frobnication is not reversible. Keep a backup, or use [yellow]--dry-run[] first.

[bold,underline]Configuration[]

Settings live in [yellow]frobnicate.toml[]:

  [[yellow]defaults[]]
  [red]jobs[] = [yellow]8[]
  [red]quiet[] = [yellow]false[]

[bold,underline]Contributing[]

Pull requests are welcome. Please run the tests first, and mention the issue
number in the title. For larger changes, open an issue to discuss the idea.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Released under the MIT license. Copyright (c) the frobnicate authors.
